# 1. What do all the methods (move(), special_move(), use()) in the previous activities have in common?
# They all use the same method names within different classes, but each method performs a different action.

# 2. How does this activity show polymorphism in a gaming context?
# It shows polymorphism because different characters and items can use the same method but produce different results depending on their class.

# 3. Can you think of other examples where the same action behaves differently depending on the character or item?
# Yes, an attack action can work differently depending on the character. A warrior uses a sword, a mage casts a spell, and an archer shoots an arrow.
